  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is U3 of #3663, with the scope that the user decided on 24 Nov 2026. The maintainer (Sgt_Hindsight) said: \"as long as we keep the 3D preview bit, im aiming to develop on that down the line\" / \"as running weirdly shape tools requires models\" / \"not just a spun profile\". Thus the old U3 (a large 2D drawing with painted flute helix lines) is replaced. The painted helix lines are dropped. Helical flutes on the 3D model are the follow-up #3908.\n\n- The editor of the tool library window has a preview area above its Tool and Details tabs. It has two views and a toggle (\"3D\" / \"Side\"):\n  - **3D (the default):** the tool as an orbitable model (drag to turn, scroll to zoom, double-click to fit). A tool with a landed body shows the steel revolved up to the body, and then the body's own facets. A tool without a body shows the steel and the holder cylinder, both revolved. Thus the view is never empty. The steel is the landed drawn cutter (`ToolCutter`, carried onto the draft numbers), else `Tool::profile` up to the shank top. A caption says where the model comes from.\n  - **Side (to scale):** the side drawing of `tool_preview` at the size of the editor, with dimension lines: diameter, flute length, shank (Ø × length), stick-out (tip to holder face), gauge (tip to holder top) and holder (Ø × length). No helix lines.\n- The renderer of the body placement view (#371) moves into its own module, `egui_app/tool_model_view.rs` (`View`, `project`, `gesture`, `apply`), so that the maintainer can build on it. The placement view uses it. Pick tip and Pick axis stay on the tool page and do not change (`placement_view`). The orbit is one value, `state::Orbit`.\n- `preview_inputs` returns a landed drawn cutter on each tab, not only under \"Draw cutter\" (#93 leftover). This also fixes the Properties preview. After the review, `preview_inputs` is in its own module, `egui_app/tool_preview_inputs.rs` (moved out of `tool_profile_page.rs`).\n- Frame cost of the Properties preview (review fix): the cutter check and its outline are a memo keyed on the draft tool value and the cutter draft points, not on `doc_version`. The piece is named `ui/properties.tool.cutter_outline` with `frame_cost::span`. A still Properties frame checks no cutter.\n- `tool_preview::draw` is split into `paint` (draws into a given rect, gives the scale) and `draw`. The Properties preview paints the same pixels as before.\n- Frame cost (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`): the model (steel, bands, mesh, mesh box, dimensions) is a memo keyed on the draft tool, the document's tool, the landed cutter and the landed body (facets by `Arc` identity). The projected screen mesh is a second memo keyed on the model mesh, the rect and the orbit. Neither keys on `doc_version`. The piece is named `ui/tool_library.preview` with `frame_cost::span`. A still frame builds and projects nothing.\n- The window's preview reads the landed body and cutter by the draft's name. It never syncs the Properties body or cutter drafts, so the window can show a different tool.\n- Display only: no command, and no law, check or post reads the preview.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3894-tool-3d-preview.md`.\n\n## Screenshots (rendered headlessly with egui_kittest on Windows)\n\n| Before (main) | After: 3D, revolved model (default) |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/before-editor.png) | ![3D revolved](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/after-3d-revolved.png) |\n\n| After: Side, with dimensions | After: 3D, imported body |\n|---|---|\n| ![side](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/after-side.png) | ![3D body](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/after-3d-body.png) |\n\n| After: Side, landed drawn cutter with a Ø 5 neck | After: Side, imported body |\n|---|---|\n| ![side neck](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/after-side-neck.png) | ![side body](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3894/after-side-body.png) |\n\n## Readings\n\n- EM-0600-4FL without a body: model radius 22.00 (holder Ø 44), cutter radius 3.00, model height 90.00 (15 + 40 + 35). Side view: stick-out 55.00, gauge 90.00, holder Ø 44.00 × 35.00.\n- Quick gate: 18 steps (all `camcraft-ui`), no app suite.\n\n## Pinning tests (new, in the ui lib, `egui_app::tests::tool_library_preview`)\n\n- `the_3d_view_is_the_default_and_shows_an_imported_body`\n- `a_tool_without_a_body_shows_a_revolved_model`\n- `a_landed_drawn_cutter_shows_in_both_views` (3D, Side and the Properties preview)\n- `the_side_view_paints_the_dimension_labels`\n- `a_still_frame_computes_no_mesh` (counters `model::builds`, `preview::projects`)\n- `a_changed_tool_rebuilds_the_mesh` (and the old input gives the old model)\n- `edit_tool_shape_in_the_window_opens_its_tool_while_properties_shows_another` (the open U2 gap)\n- `properties_still_frame_computes_no_cutter_outline` (review fix; counter `tool_preview_inputs::checks`; red on 8a7519e59: 3 computes in 3 still frames)\n- `properties_changed_tool_computes_the_cutter_outline_once` (review fix; red on 8a7519e59: 3 computes, expected 1)\n\nUpdated: `layout_window_tool_editor` (the \"3D\" toggle stands between the heading and the tabs). The helpers of `tool_library_editor` are now `pub(super)`. No test is removed, ignored or changed in its assertions otherwise. No snapshot PNG changes. No new top-level test binary.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild, final head 4ed09c9f7; it merges cleanly with origin/main 582981bfa)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 18 steps, 18 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 6.1 min. `ui suites: lib`: 1606 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored (the 9 new tests pass).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The two review tests ran red on the test commit 3505c51d5 (no memo) and green on 4ed09c9f7.\n- No heavy step: P4, display only, not under the safety floor.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Orbit, zoom and fit gestures in the library window by a real pointer (the tests pin the cache and the model, not the drag).\n- A lathe-frame body in the library window (it shows its facets over the revolved steel, as `tool_body_view::assembly` does).\n- macOS and Linux builds (Windows only).\n\n## Notes\n\n- `tool_profile_page.rs` was 412 lines on main and is 370 lines now: `preview_inputs` moved to `tool_preview_inputs.rs` (95 lines).\n- The UI has its own 20-line `revolve`, because `app::tool_body_view::revolve` is `pub(crate)`. A change in `crates/app` would add the app suites to the gate for a display-only change. The decision file records this.\n\nChangelog: The tool library window shows the tool as an orbitable 3D model (its imported body, or a model revolved from its profile) and as a to-scale side view with dimension lines. The tool preview shows a drawn cutter.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3894\n\n",
